					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-12271885#post-4373638</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-12271885/tower-b#post-4373638</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Mon, 23 Sep 2019 23:41:43 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Bassoe</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>3070028</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>I'm confused. Did&#8230;<br /> • &#8230;Balestri commit suicide by breaching the depressurization chamber to take his mutated spinal column with him.<br /> • &#8230;the depressurization chamber handler see Balestri's spine emerging from his body through the chamber porthole and breach the chamber to kill it.<br /> • &#8230;Balestri's spine emerge from his body, see the handler through the porthole and breach the chamber by trying to escape it and attack the handler.<br /> In any case, whose spine was the Sea Centipede? Balestri's was presumably still in his body when the narrator saw it, he chatted with the narrator afterwards. Was there a native population of mutant ambulatory spines/Sea Centipedes living on the seabed even before the oil rig was built? Where'd they come from?</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
